Original Zero compiler provenance and active seed

The active application seed is bootstrap/zero64.zapp, an original Zero compiler
image with the ZEROAPP1 ABI header. tools/build.zero validates it, compiles the
canonical compiler.zero source and checks successive app generations for exact
self-reproduction before producing artifacts.

Use zero-build PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY. The output directory
must not exist. Source composition is performed by tools/integrate.zero; neither
step calls a foreign compiler, assembler, linker, script or interpreter.
Read tools/build.ztext and tools/integrate.ztext with zero-text.

Early bootstrap work originally used our own assembly implementation, followed
by an original Zero compiler and an original Zero arena adjustment. That is
provenance, not a current build dependency. Historical transition helpers and
reports do not constitute a current release test; active source is Zero/Ezero.
The current seed and source identity must be recorded with each verified build.
